\documentclass{article}
\title{Weak Instruments in Applied Econometrics}
\author{D. Nakamura}
\date{May 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Motivation}
Instrumental variables recover causal effects when the treatment of interest is endogenous.
The main threats to a credible design are well known:
\begin{itemize}
\item instruments that move the outcome through channels other than the treatment;
\item first stages that are too weak to shift the treatment in a meaningful way;
\item heterogeneous effects that complicate the interpretation of the estimand.
\section{Empirical Strategy}
We report first stage F statistics for every specification we estimate,
and we rotate across candidate instruments as a robustness exercise.
\end{document}

